{"artifact_id":"extract_58a344895827c21413881093","byte_end":232998,"byte_start":229445,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.1","original_html":"<p id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">For the sphaleron signal, a limit on the cross section can be converted into a limit on the pre-exponential factor, defined in Section\u00a0<a href=\"#Ch0.S3\" title='0.3 Data and simulated samples \u2023 A search for microscopic black holes, string balls, and sphalerons in proton-proton collisions at \u221a\ud835\udc60=13\u2062\"ERROR \\TeV\"' class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">0.3</span></a>. Following the method in Ref.\u00a0<cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib17\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">17</a>]</cite>, we calculate the limits on the pre-exponential factor for five scanned <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math> values: 8.5, 8.75, 9, 9.25, 9.5<span id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>, under the assumptions of <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p({N_{\\text{CS}}})=0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p({N_{\\text{CS}}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0.5\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>. The observed and expected 95% <span id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.1.2\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\CL</span>upper limits on the pre-exponential factor as functions of <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math> are shown in Fig.\u00a0<a href=\"#Ch0.F12\" title='Figure 12 \u2023 0.9.2 Model-dependent results \u2023 0.9 Results \u2023 A search for microscopic black holes, string balls, and sphalerons in proton-proton collisions at \u221a\ud835\udc60=13\u2062\"ERROR \\TeV\"' class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">12</span></a>.\nThe observed (expected) upper limit for the nominal <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}=9\\TeV\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}=9\\TeV</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p9.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p({N_{\\text{CS}}})=0.5\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p({N_{\\text{CS}}})=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> is 0.0034 (0.0035), which is approximately 6.2 (3.4) times more stringent than the previous best limit of 0.021 (0.012) from CMS\u00a0<cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib21\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">21</a>]</cite>.</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"7fadcfce5fce60055ccd817d98d05c9d09e4c759f1691022a0d3f4f7cf2be955","source_id":"cms_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.10732v2"}